A||||3||My7Fieros||Whats the average running temp for an 84 duke?||||1||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||11-17-2001||05:57 PM||||Courious...bought my first 4 banger Fiero (Indy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )...havnt driven it yet, needs a couple of minor things done first, but was courious. Also what temp does the fan kick on? (I know about the V6's, but like I said, this is my first duke). Thanx||||reg||1
Z||000001||William Federle||11-17-2001||06:14 PM||||I have a 1984 SE. I have my fan on continuously and I have a 180 deg. thermostat. My car runs at 190 deg all of the time, except on very hot days in the summer, when it gets up to 200 deg and maybe a little warmer. On my temperature gage, I've confirmed with a separate temp gage that the first mark (about 1/4 full scale) from the left is approx. 190 deg.<P>I think that the temp switch on the engine block that turns on the fan normally closes at about 235 deg F.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||11-17-2001||08:13 PM||||The above info is correct.  I also have a 180 degree thermo and have my fan on a manual switch so I can use it when I want.  Runs at the first mark on the gauge most of the time.||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||11-17-2001||08:54 PM||||Sounds good, thanks!||||reg||14
